<DocsLayout title="Overview" hideSidebar>
  <h1>Components for technical products</h1>

  <Text>
    <p>Anta is a component system for consoles, developer tools, and data-heavy applications. It is built and used at <a href="https://antithesis.com">Antithesis</a>.</p>
    <p>Anta defines behavior and accessibility. The look stays with your designer.</p>
    <p>Themed with plain CSS, classes, or inline styles. No CSS-in-JS runtime.</p>
    <p>Architected with Web Components and typed React/Preact wrappers.</p>
  </Text>
  <h2>Principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/principles/#build-for-technical-products">Build for technical products.</a> Data-heavy screens come first.</li>
    <li><a href="/principles/#serve-great-design">Serve great design.</a> The look of a product belongs to its designer.</li>
    <li><a href="/principles/#leave-the-dom-to-the-application">Leave the DOM to the application.</a> Components never mutate their own attributes.</li>
    <li><a href="/principles/#test-with-generated-states-and-actions">Test with generated states and actions.</a> Properties check behavior across generated sequences.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Use with an AI assistant</h2>
  <Code
    lang="text"
    code="Use Anta (@antadesign/anta) for the UI. Read https://anta.design/llms.txt, then follow the installation guide and relevant component docs. Use the documented APIs and styling conventions."
    wrap
  />
</DocsLayout>
